Full `test-system "clautolisp"`: 5482 checks, Fail 0.

Measured on real AutoCAD (2026-09-26)
--------------------------------------
vendor:probes:autocad (MR !292 native child 2885828771, AutoCAD 2022
accoreconsole/Windows) reports the drawing-data probe DIVERGED — recorded,
not gated — with the whole xdata payload absent on AutoCAD:

    UNEXPECTED  xdata.surfaced-with-applist: no,  expected yes
    UNEXPECTED  xdata.pair-count:            0,   expected 8
    UNEXPECTED  xdata.1000-string:           no,  expected yes
    UNEXPECTED  xdata.1040-real:             no,  expected yes
    UNEXPECTED  xdata.1070-int16:            no,  expected yes
    UNEXPECTED  xdata.1071-int32:            no,  expected yes
    UNEXPECTED  xdata.1005-handle:           no,  expected yes
    (20 conforms, 7 unexpected, 0 missing)

So an xdata payload attached in the probe does not read back through
ENTGET on AutoCAD accoreconsole (the same probe conforms on BricsCAD and
clautolisp). This is the concrete AutoCAD end of the XData-fidelity work
above — the REGAPP/1001-applist + full group-code round-trip is what is
failing to surface. entity-lifecycle and selection probes PASS on the same
run, so it is xdata-specific, not a general entget breakage.


Answered 2026-10-03 -- the AutoCAD xdata "divergence" was the probe's handle
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
probes/sources/probe-xdata.lsp (MR !378) attached each group of the
drawing-data payload alone. AutoCAD 2022 (20261003T142717Z) VALIDATES two
groups on ENTMOD and rejects the whole call -- returns nil, attaches
nothing -- when:
  - a 1005 handle names no object (the drawing-data probe used "2A");
  - a 1003 names a layer that does not exist.
The payload without the dangling 1005 reads back all 7 pairs on AutoCAD.
BricsCAD (20261003T142514Z) accepts the dangling handle, and for the
missing layer returns the list but silently DROPS the xdata.

So the probe, not AutoCAD's xdata support, was at fault, and clautolisp
was wrong to accept everything. Fixed in clautolisp 2.2.157:
  - cador ENTMOD vets xdata: AutoCAD's rule by default (and strict),
    BricsCAD's under a BricsCAD dialect (deviant policy). probe-xdata
    now equals AutoCAD 24/24 and, under --dialect bricscad-mac, BricsCAD
    24/24. Test dd-xdata-entmod-checks-handles-and-layers-as-the-vendors-do.
  - The drawing-data probe (.lsp + the three scenario .sexp copies) and the
    dd-xdata-full-codeset test now use a handle that EXISTS (the circle's
    own) and layer "0", so the round-trip is portable.
LEFT before closing: one run of the fixed drawing-data probe on AutoCAD
(its vendor family runs on the push), expecting the 8 pairs at last.
